# WinForms designer safety (SmartMed.UI)

## Control BackColor
- Never set `Color.Transparent` or alpha &lt; 255 on `TextBox`, `Panel`, `Button`, or other `Control.BackColor`.
- Use `ThemeApplier.SetBackColor(control, color)` or `AppTheme.EnsureOpaque(color)` instead of raw `Color.FromArgb(a,r,g,b)` when `a < 255`.
- For inputs on primary panels use `ThemeApplier.ApplyTextBoxOnPrimary(textBox)`.
- Semi-transparent colors (`AppTheme.HeaderHover`, `OnPrimaryMuted`) are for `ForeColor` or runtime-only `MouseOverBackColor`, not `BackColor`.

## Inherited admin forms (AdminShellForm)
- `AdminShellForm` must be a registered Form (`SubType>Form</SubType>`, `.resx`, public parameterless constructor).
- Each admin page form must have `FormName.Designer.cs` that calls `InitializeComponent()` from the derived ctor (after `base(...)`).
- Set `lblTopSubtitle.Text` in the derived `Designer.cs` `InitializeComponent()` so the VS designer shows the correct page title.
- Do **not** build `panelContent` in the constructor. `AdminShellForm.OnLoad` calls `EnsurePageContent()` → `InitializePageContent()` once `DesignMode` is reliable.
- Use `IsDesignHost()` (from `AdminShellForm`) — not `LicenseManager.UsageMode` alone — to detect the VS designer.
- Never open database connections, repositories, or services in the designer. Guard with `if (IsDesignHost()) return null` or skip `Load*()` calls.

## Code-built page content (Manage Medicines, Customers, etc.)
- Override `InitializePageContent()`: call `BuildPageContent()` once (`_pageBuilt` guard).
- `BuildPageContent()` must call `BuildContent()` then `LoadDesignTimePreview()` when `IsDesignHost()`.
- `LoadDesignTimePreview()` is chrome-only (empty grids / "—" stats). Do not load mock rows or open services.
- Runtime data load (`LoadMedicines()`, etc.) runs only when `!IsDesignHost()`.
- Stats, expiry alerts, and grid formatting must not require `MedicineService` / DB when `IsDesignHost()` is true.

## Designer / runtime parity checklist
When changing an admin page UI, verify all of the following:
1. Designer shows the same controls as runtime (grid, search, form, stats, alerts).
2. `lblTopSubtitle` matches the page name in both designer and runtime.
3. `LoadDesignTimePreview()` stays empty of sample data (chrome / blank only).
4. No service/repository is constructed during design time.
5. `AutoScaleDimensions` stays `7F, 15F` on all admin forms (match `AdminShellForm`).
6. Do not save stale `btnClose` / `btnNavLogout` positions in Designer files; anchors + `SyncShellChrome()` own placement.

## After UI changes
- Rebuild the project, close and reopen the form in the VS designer if `panelContent` still looks empty.
- If the designer is blank but runtime works, check that page build is deferred to `OnLoad`, not the constructor.
